In article <1724@yenta.alb.nm.us> dt@yenta.alb.nm.us (David B. Thomas) writes:
>When I read a scroll of identify, it asks what I wish to identify, and
>suggests [!)* a]   However, if I indicate 'a' it identifies item 'a'
>in my inventory and no more scroll.  Is there a way, short of copying
>the list of category symbols !)*, that you can ask the game to prompt
>you for each item?  Would 'A' work?
>
>					The Other David

Apologies in advance for not answering your question.  I think it would
be much nicer if the game just prompted you for a single item to identify
at a time.  This only matters when the identify scroll gives you multiple
identifications.  The current prompting mechanism is a pain because the
results are too dependent on pack order.


